        <ArticleTitle>Antimicrobial activity of nisin against Listeria monocytogenes in broth microdilution assay.</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND">Listeria monocytogenes is a major foodborne pathogen.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="RESULTS">In a broth microdilution assay, 10^6 CFU/mL Listeria monocytogenes in BHI broth was exposed to nisin at 2.5 mg/L. The MIC of nisin was 2.5 mg/L at pH 6.5.</AbstractText>
